  "circulation": "Administration/day-room loop provides a short return. East wet-treatment loop has two independent doors. West passage connects ward, chapel and garden exit; patient wards remain ordinary inhabited-space histories with protected personal accounts.",
  "systems": "Wet-room water, boiler heat and ward ventilation produce normal baselines. Separate ward and clinical circuits avoid a single inexplicable all-building switch. Court light and window sightlines orient both players and later allies.",
  "campaign": "Case files and staff correspondence present conflicting testimony respectfully. Neither diagnoses nor treatment history prescribe ghost hostility or evidence.",
  "refine": [
    "Staggered ward concept informed by primary DC planning brochure; inspect actual floor drawings before detailed construction.",
    "Add believable sanitary/service rooms as child spaces; preserve broad corridor turn clearance.",
    "Draw basement stairs and evacuation route; avoid an upper ward with a single untelegraphed trap."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "docs/environments/ROOM_AND_ASSET_REQUIREMENTS.md",
    "https://planning.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/op/publication/attachments/St%20Elizabeths%20Brochure.pdf (indexed text inspected 2026-10-21; wards staggered for light; dimensions authored)"
  ]
